.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A segmented cache implementation that splits a large logical address space into multiple fixed-size cache segments\&. 
.br
 The first segment is the base \fBCache\fP instance, while all additional segments are stored in an internal array of \fBICache\fP\&. 

This class supports large continuous write operations by automatically determining the correct segment and offset for each write\&. 
.br
 Writes may span multiple segments, and data is written chunk-by-chunk using a temporary \fBFixedVector<T>\fP buffer\&. 
.PP
